  "final": "Done. All checks pass.\n\n## Changes\n\n**New: `src/exporter.py`** — the single shared entry point:\n- `export_rows(rows, format)` raises `ValueError(\"unsupported format\")` for anything other than `'csv'`/`'json'`.\n- `_normalize(rows)` materializes rows exactly once into a new list (so one-shot generators work and inputs aren't mutated), keeping only `id`/`name` in order, mapping missing or `None` to `''` and stringifying everything else.\n- CSV branch: `csv.writer` on `io.StringIO(newline=\"\")` with `lineterminator=\"\\n\"` (LF endings, standard quoting), always writes the `id,name` header even for zero rows.\n- JSON branch: `json.dumps(..., ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\",\", \":\"))`.\n\n**`src/csv_exporter.py` / `src/json_exporter.py`** — all duplicated normalization and serialization loops removed; each is now a one-line delegation to `export_rows(rows, \"csv\" | \"json\")`, returning byte-identical strings to before.\n\n**`src/dispatcher.py`** — untouched; it still routes `export()` through the two public wrappers, which now funnel into the shared implementation.\n\n**`checks/exporter.py`** (new) — covers wrapper/entry-point equivalence, empty-rows header rules, one-shot generators, input non-mutation, `None`/missing → `''`, value stringification, unicode + compact JSON separators, and `ValueError` on unsupported formats (including case-sensitive `\"CSV\"`).\n\n## Verification\n- `python3 checks/public.py` — passes (exercises the dispatcher end-to-end).\n- `python3 checks/exporter.py` — passes all additional edge cases.",
